# Loom renders per-machine agent definitions into ~/.pi/agent/agents. Until the
# home-manager migration turns that path into a real directory, those renders
# land here. They are machine-bound (absolute package roots, inlined skill
# bodies) and go stale on every Loom commit — home-manager regenerates them via
# scripts/sync-pi-agents.sh, and Loom's pre-tool-use guard rejects any file that
# is not the current render. They must never be committed.
#
# Only this repo's own generic agents are tracked; everything else is ignored.
*
!.gitignore
!planner.md
!reviewer.md
!scout.md
!worker.md
